.TH QFW-QPM-SVC 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-qpm-svc \- manage one QFw QPM service instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-qpm-svc
.I start|run
.B --run-dir
.I path
.B --service-id
.I id
[
.I options
]
.PP
.B qfw-qpm-svc
.I status|stop
.B --run-dir
.I path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-qpm-svc
starts, supervises, inspects, or stops exactly one QPM and its optional PRTE
DVM. It reads directory connection information automatically from the site
configuration or from
.BR --directory-service-info .
.PP
In application scope QPMd and the PRTE DVM master run on the head of
allocation group 1. In site scope
.B --node
selects the QPM node. Remote placement requires a Slurm allocation.
.PP
.BR qfw-setup (1)
invokes this lifecycle engine once for each QPM selected by an application
runtime profile. It passes the directory connection record automatically and
.BR qfw-teardown (1)
stops the recorded managers in reverse order.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B start
Start in the background and return after QPM readiness.
.TP
.B run
Remain in the foreground for a service supervisor. SIGINT and SIGTERM stop the
QPM and then its owned DVM.
.TP
.B status
Probe recorded components and print generated state as JSON.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the QPM and optional DVM in reverse order and update generated state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --run-dir " path"
Private lifecycle state, PID, readiness, DVM URI, and log directory.
.TP
.BI --service-id " id"
The single service manifest entry managed by this instance. The option may be
specified only once.
.TP
.BI --directory-service-info " path"
Override the client-readable directory connection record. Site scope normally
obtains this path from
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5).
.TP
.BI --site-config " path"
Site configuration.
.TP
.BI --runtime-config " path"
Runtime configuration.
.TP
.BI --scope " application|site"
Select application-owned or site-owned lifetime and placement rules.
.TP
.BI --node " node"
Site-scope QPM node. This option is rejected in application scope.
.TP
.BI --timeout " seconds"
Startup and directory-registration timeout. The default is 120 seconds.
.TP
.BI --poll-interval " seconds"
Foreground supervision interval used by
.BR run .
The default is 2 seconds.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Resolve and record the plan without starting processes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful startup, ready status, or shutdown. Status returns
nonzero when the QPM or its owned DVM is not ready. Configuration, readiness,
and cleanup errors also return nonzero.
